# Wireworm — Debug and automation surface

{{#if (eq engine.slug "none")}}
Wireworm carries a debugging and automation surface, `window.__wireworm`, so the
game can be driven and inspected from code without holding a key or waiting on
real time.

You implement it. Every operation this file specifies is a deliverable, and the
build installs the finished surface on `window.__wireworm` as soon as the game
has initialized. Every scenario driven from code reaches the game through it, so
it is present and exactly as specified here.

Each operation is a read of the game's state, a pose of one field of it, or a
move of the clock. A pose arranges the board, and the game's own stepping,
collision, charge, discharge, and scoring rules run from there exactly as they do
in play, so a scenario driven from code behaves exactly like one played by hand.

The surface is inert during normal play, doing nothing until something calls it.
{{else if (eq engine.slug "simple-2d")}}
